, the median FWCI is 0–0.24. In every year, half of the works received at most 24% of the citations expected for similar works worldwide (FWCI 1 = world average).","Above the world average: 0%–33% of the works per year have an FWCI above 1, most in 2019 (33%).","Not cited: on average 79% of these works have FWCI 0, meaning no citations within their four-year window. That is why many boxes start at 0.","Mean versus median: the mean is above the median in 5 of 8 years, because a few highly cited works pull the average up. The widest gap is 2019: mean 0.8, median 0, top work 3.81. The median is the better guide to a typical work.","Small base: the values for 2010–2013, 2017 and 2019–2021 are based on only 10–29 works (lighter box or hollow point), so read them with care.","Few works: 2015, 2018, 2022 and 2025 have fewer than 10 works, too few for a box. Each of those works is drawn as a dot."],"citations":["Typical work: works published 2010–2021 have a median of 0.5–3.5 citations each; the highest median (3.5) is in 2013.","Most cited works: the top 10% of works published in 2011 have at least 11.4 citations each, the highest P90 in the chart.","Mean versus median: the mean is above the median in 7 of 8 years, because a few highly cited works pull the average up. The widest gap is 2021: mean 2.6, median 1, top work 16. The median is the better guide to a typical work.","Small base: the values for 2010–2013, 2017 and 2019–2021 are based on only 10–29 works (lighter box or hollow point), so read them with care.","Few works: 2015, 2018, 2022 and 2025 have fewer than 10 works, too few for a band. Each of those works is drawn as a dot."]}}}